{"seq":31,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:40:25.415Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"201f8814cc28af4e0248f86bfbfc2efc400ab3ece4a4c0522f69c4bc363fb66e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, I found six ticket references on Vantorre Group (the parent) in the pod channel, #inc-vtg-hartford and Moss's Strategic digests. I left out Mobility's #4812 and QFO's #PD-4402.\n\n| Ticket | What it is | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#8841** (also written **#PD-8841**) | Gate and kiosk issues at Vantorre's plants. | 1. Moss digest 4/27/26: \"#PD-8841\", two missed carrier check-ins at Allentown, Gate 4, 2nd shift.<br>2. Moss digest 5/4/26: \"#8841\", still open, gate kiosk timeout at Allentown, Door 12.<br>3. #strategic-pod, 7/1/26, Gideon: closed with support.<br>4. Moss digest 9/30/26: \"#8841\", Mateo submitted it, drivers can't select Door 14 at the Newark facility, escalated to platform engineering. |\n| **#PD-4418** | `Carrier_Dwell_Summary` export dropping timestamps for Dock Door 9 at the 04:00 shift change. | Moss digest 9/15/25. It says \"the account Nadia runs\" and doesn't name Vantorre. I'm counting it as VTG because of the 5/4/26 handoff digest, so please confirm. |\n| **INC-4821** | Mateo's access-denied problem on the status page during the Hartford outage. | #inc-vtg-hartford, 8/3/26, Gideon at 11:08, screenshot attached. |\n| **VT-55120** | Root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage. It holds Carrowmere's gateway route finding and the reconnect log. | #inc-vtg-hartford, 10/14/26, Gideon. I haven't seen the ticket itself. |\n\n**Things to check before this goes to Mateo:**\n- **#8841 doesn't line up.**\n  - Gideon closed it on 7/1, but the 9/30 digest has Mateo submitting it as new.\n  - The site is Allentown in April, May and July, and Newark in September.\n  - It may be one ticket reopened, or a number reused. I can't tell from what I can read, so I'd confirm in the support system.\n  - Treating #PD-8841 and #8841 as the same ticket is my assumption.\n- **Some entries have no number.**\n  - The 8/3/26 digest covers the Hartford Sev 1 and the door-assignment and duplicate check-in complaints, with no ticket number.\n  - The 5/3/26 digest mentions duplicate arrivals at door 14 and \"the existing support thread\", also with no number.\n  - The 3/10/25 digest has Mateo's email about Allentown gate delays, which isn't a ticket.\n- **I haven't opened the ticketing system.** This list only covers what's written in those three places, so tickets that were never mentioned there won't be on it."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
